{
  "schema_version": "partial-dates.v1",
  "description": "Shared test dates for every copy of the partial-date validators, under stage 1 of the deep-time date format (docs/development/deep-time-date-format-brief-2026-11-24.md, rulings 1 to 8 of section 10). A partial date is YYYY, YYYY-MM or YYYY-MM-DD with ASCII digits and a real Gregorian calendar date. Each row says whether the value is valid as a historical date and as an observation date, whether it has the digit shape the JSON schemas check (form), and, when it is a valid historical date, the first and last calendar day it covers.",
  "kinds": {
    "historical": "A date when something happened at a place: the bounds of a dated claim, the start and end of a period, a date in a function chain, the lifecycle date. Any real date from the year 0001; the country's floor applies on top, with a confirmation below it.",
    "observation": "A date when evidence was made: an observation, a photograph, a source's own date. A real date from 1000 to 2100; a documentary source's date below 1000 takes a confirmation.",
    "form": "The digit shape alone, as the JSON schema patterns check it: four digits, then optionally two and two, joined by hyphens. Year, month and day ranges are left to the validators."
  },
